---
source: crates/pogo-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: help
---
Read bytes from a device, optionally from a register

Usage: pogo i2c read [OPTIONS] --len <LEN> <ADDR>

Arguments:
  <ADDR>
          

Options:
      --reg <REG>
          Register to read from (write then repeated-start read)

      --len <LEN>
          Number of bytes to read

      --bus <BUS>
          [default: 0]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
  -d, --device <SELECTOR>
          Target device: alias, USB serial, port, or "auto"

      --probe <SELECTOR>
          Probe device [default: "probe" alias, else auto]

  -f, --format <FORMAT>
          Output format [default: human]
          
          [env: POGO_FORMAT=]
          [possible values: human, json, jsonl]

      --config <PATH>
          Config file
          
          [env: POGO_CONFIG=]

      --timeout <DURATION>
          Overall deadline for this command, e.g. 500ms, 10s, 2m

      --wait-lock <DURATION>
          Wait for a busy device instead of failing

      --dry-run
          Describe what a mutating command would do; change nothing

  -v, --verbose...
          More logs on stderr (repeatable)

  -q, --quiet
          Errors only on stderr

      --no-color
          Disable colors

Requires the probe. With --reg, writes the register address then does a repeated-start read.

Examples:
  pogo i2c read 0x68 --reg 0x75 --len 1
  pogo i2c read 0x76 --reg 0xd0 --len 1 -f json

Exit codes: 0 ok, 3 probe not found, 6 probe I/O, NACK, or protocol

JSON data: { bus, addr, reg, bytes_hex, bytes_dec }
